-    *   Weight and sum the noise components per pixel to create a displacement vector field (for coordinate perturbation) or a modulation vector (for property perturbation) [S2, S3].
-    *   *Note:* Low-frequency perturbation is achieved by applying the texture once with large amplitude [S2]. High-frequency perturbation is achieved by applying the texture again with low amplitude and allowing the texture to repeat [S2].
